<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>“<strong>Tech Debt</strong>” sounds bad and something to avoid.   But, that risk averse viewpoint can be crippling.    </p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>In fact it is our ally to successfully developing high quality software.  I’ll explain this later, but first you need to know what it is, and why we have it.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Read this GitHub article <strong><a href="https://github.com/resources/articles/what-is-technical-debt" data-type="link" data-id="https://github.com/resources/articles/what-is-technical-debt">What is technical debt</a></strong>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Now leave some comments below about why I say that <strong>Technical Debt</strong> can be a valuable tool.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->
